# === Loop runtime state (regenerated by host/verify_loop*.mjs) ===
# sshd host keys, the generated sshd_config, its log, and the raw packet
# captures. Everything in here is derived; nothing here is source.
.loop*/

# === Generated package interfaces ===
# The toolchain writes `pkg.generated.mbti` for EVERY package on EVERY
# build. Measured on moon 0.1.20261102; the previous version wrote one
# only for the packages `moon info` had been asked for, which is why
# this list used to name two entries instead of one rule.
#
# The interfaces this repository treats as claims are TRACKED, and a
# .gitignore does not untrack them: this rule only decides what happens
# to the ones that are not tracked, which are the toolchain's per-build
# output rather than part of the source.  Leaving them untracked and
# unignored is not an option either -- 51 permanently dirty files, and
# `ci/ci.py --tag` refuses to tag a dirty tree.
#
# The two entries this rule replaces -- src/sshclient and src/wtlive --
# were excluded because "the generated interface drifts with the target".
# That was a measurement, not an assumption, and it no longer
# reproduces: built for native, js, wasm and wasm-gc in turn, all four
# produce a byte-identical file (sha256 26f351b4850b and 88c147329e46).
# A rule whose stated reason has stopped being true is a rule that
# stops being reviewed, so it is gone rather than kept for its shape.
**/pkg.generated.mbti

# === Third-party vendored source (keep) ===
# Do NOT ignore *.c, *.h, *.py, *.json in src/ and verify_c/ etc.

# === CI run artifacts (a report from one run, not source) ===
# ci/artifacts/ci.json changes on every run; committing it turns a
# CI report into a diff in an unrelated loop.
ci/artifacts/
